msgid "This site has more than one podcast. Choose the one to set up now; the steps about its data and its platforms will work on it. You can change it at any time from the top of this page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:44
msgid "This is the identity of your podcast: the name, description, cover and category that Apple Podcasts, Spotify and the other apps show. Without them your feed is incomplete and the platforms may reject it. The fields at the bottom (copyright, type and website) are optional."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:49
#: includes/class-settings.php:476
msgid "Episode titles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:50
msgid "Here you choose how the title of each episode is built: a prefix such as «Episode», the season and how episodes are counted. If you leave it as it is, episodes get the title the AI writes, without a prefix or a number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:55
#: includes/class-settings.php:597
msgid "How your podcast writes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:56
msgid "VozCaster can write the title, excerpt, post and chapters of each episode with AI. A style guide tells it how your podcast sounds: serious, funny, formal, relaxed. If you leave it empty, the AI copies the tone it hears in your recording."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:61
#: includes/class-settings.php:651
msgid "Post footer (signature)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:62
msgid "A text that VozCaster adds at the end of every post it publishes: who you are, how to contact you, where to subscribe. If you leave it empty, nothing is added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:67
msgid "Cover images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:68
msgid "Episode covers can be drawn with AI. You can ask for a recurring element in all of them (an orange cat with headphones, say) and give a reference image whose style the covers copy. By default each cover is inspired only by the text of the episode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:73
#: includes/class-settings.php:767
msgid "AI content notice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:74
msgid "When a post is written with AI, a short notice says so, which your readers will appreciate. It is on by default. You can change its wording and position, and turn on a small «Published with VozCaster» credit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:78
#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:84
#: includes/class-settings.php:62
msgid "Audio"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:79
msgid "Intro, outro and separator"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:80
msgid "The intro and the outro are short pieces of music that open and close every episode. The separator is a short sound used between the parts of an episode recorded in several audios. Without them, your episodes have just your voice and several audios are joined with a one-second pause."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:85
msgid "Music mix"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:86
msgid "How the music blends with your voice: when the intro starts to fade, how loud it stays under your voice and when the outro comes in. The defaults suit most music and you can change them later. It only matters if you uploaded an intro or an outro."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:90
#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:91
msgid "Who can publish"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:92
msgid "Choose who can publish in each podcast of this site, and who only sends episodes for review before they go out. By default every role that can publish posts (administrators, editors, authors) publishes directly. If you work alone, you can keep it as it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:96
#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:97
msgid "Groups and reviewers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:98
msgid "A podcast can have groups, each one with its own reviewers: the sections of a team or the members of an association, for example. What a member sends for review reaches the reviewers of their group, and each group gets its own page and feed. If you do not need groups, skip this step; you can add them later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:104
msgid "Link your account with VozCaster so you can send voice notes from Telegram or from the web app. It takes one click and you can connect again whenever you want."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-guided-setup.php:110
msgid "When your podcast has at least one published episode, you can send its feed to Apple Podcasts, Spotify and the rest. You do it once per platform; after that they pick up every new episode by themselves."
msgstr ""

